1
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:38,180
[First Love Again]

2
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:40,970
[Episode 2]

3
00:01:47,479 --> 00:01:48,680
Sorry, sorry.

4
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:02,880
No need to thank me.

5
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:04,800
Are you crazy?

6
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:16,760
You're slacking off.

7
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:22,280
I'm here to borrow books, okay?

8
00:02:22,950 --> 00:02:23,880
I hope so.

9
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:38,910
[Marketing]

10
00:02:38,910 --> 00:02:39,620
[The Essence of Marketing]

11
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:43,360
Xiangxiang.

12
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:46,370
How did your chat
with Senior Fang Yu go today?

13
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:52,490
First the elective course,

14
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:54,240
then the group assignment,

15
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,600
and then the library.

16
00:02:56,079 --> 00:02:58,360
Why am I never brave enough?

17
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,800
Was it that bad?

18
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:04,920
Forget I asked.

19
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:12,230
[Gu Han]

20
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:15,760
Here are some past survey report samples.

21
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:16,560
Study them.

22
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:18,400
Before tomorrow's meeting,

23
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,800
go buy 200 yuan worth of snacks.

24
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:21,020
[Gu Han]

25
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:20,800
No repeats.

26
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:23,480
200 yuan for snacks with no repeats?

27
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:25,200
That's really weird.

28
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:26,600
Here, coffee.

29
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,960
You two really are on the same wavelength.

30
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,320
Xiangxiang stayed up late,

31
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:32,850
so a coffee will perk her up.

32
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:35,840
Thank you, Senior.

33
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:37,360
Here.

34
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:39,760
Continue.

35
00:03:52,630 --> 00:03:54,630
[Selection of Quantitative
Research Methods]

36
00:04:03,990 --> 00:04:07,870
[Gu Han]

37
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:05,560
Stay focused.

38
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:13,320
Is he hiding somewhere

39
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:15,040
and secretly watching me?

40
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:23,080
How is it?

41
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:25,080
The taste

42
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:26,840
is quite special.

43
00:05:27,610 --> 00:05:28,320
Idiot.

44
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:31,140
Do you really not remember anything?

45
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:01,930
How long have you been here?

46
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:04,290
I've been here for over an hour.

47
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:12,320
I didn't expect to sleep this long.

48
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:13,720
You're drooling.

49
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:18,320
I'm not drooling.

50
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:20,880
Are you crazy?

51
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:25,600
Since you're awake, memorize these.

52
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:30,160
It's so thick.

53
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:32,080
We start our research tomorrow.

54
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,260
How can I memorize it all?

55
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:35,260
Do you still want to be in the top 80%?

56
00:07:04,290 --> 00:07:05,760
After recording the slow-moving products,

57
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:07,040
restock the new goods.

58
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:08,400
That way,

59
00:07:08,430 --> 00:07:10,280
it helps you better understand
customer needs,

60
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:12,400
and you can help the shop owner
restock too.

61
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:13,820
This should all be in the notes

62
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:14,720
I gave you yesterday.

63
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,520
I read them.

64
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,760
Take instant noodles, for example.

65
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:18,740
Sort them by brand,

66
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:20,080
imported or domestic,

67
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:20,880
and by flavor,

68
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:21,600
spicy or non-spicy.

69
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:22,680
Like that, right?

70
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:28,760
Are you hungry?

71
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:33,720
Here.

72
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:38,240
Thank you.

73
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:43,200
How did he know I like this flavor?

74
00:07:46,810 --> 00:07:48,360
It just occurred to me—

75
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:50,780
asking me to buy different snacks
every day

76
00:07:50,780 --> 00:07:52,180
actually really helped.

77
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:55,320
I know where everything is here.

78
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:58,840
Mr. Gu is quite impressive.

79
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:13,840
Here.

80
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:15,480
Thank you.

81
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:30,560
Delicious.

82
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:38,340
[Jiangcheng University Basketball Team]

83
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:37,559
Come on, hurry up.

84
00:08:37,559 --> 00:08:38,559
Move, move!

85
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:40,130
Execute tactic number one!

86
00:08:40,210 --> 00:08:40,980
[Jiangcheng University Basketball Team]

87
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,360
Pass it, pass it!

88
00:08:42,799 --> 00:08:43,360
Good!

89
00:08:44,090 --> 00:08:45,550
Pass the ball, Zhou Yunze!

90
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:48,760
Zhou Yunze.

91
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:51,160
Your job is to get offensive rebounds,

92
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:52,240
not to shoot.

93
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,520
Why didn't you pass?

94
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:56,430
I already had deep post position—

95
00:08:56,430 --> 00:08:57,650
perfect chance to put it up.

96
00:08:57,650 --> 00:08:59,080
You didn't pass to Gu Han,

97
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,120
and if you miss,

98
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:01,780
we'll just get hit on a fast break.

99
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:02,760
Understand?

100
00:09:03,310 --> 00:09:04,360
Coach Chu.

101
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:05,680
I don't get it.

102
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:07,120
Why does every single possession

103
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:08,400
have to go through him?

104
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,200
I had great position down low,

105
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,640
and you could've just given me the ball.

106
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:12,560
I can post up,

107
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:13,320
go one-on-one,

108
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,150
or facilitate.

109
00:09:14,150 --> 00:09:15,320
Your skills aren't that good.

110
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,280
What did you say?

111
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:18,760
Gu Han, don't think

112
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:19,880
you win scoring champion every year

113
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:21,360
because you're some superstar.

114
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:23,690
It's because everyone gives you the ball.

115
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,410
If you were good enough,

116
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:28,200
you wouldn't be stuck
in the quarterfinals every year.

117
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:28,960
Zhou Yunze.

118
00:09:29,370 --> 00:09:30,560
It's better to put

119
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:32,690
the group survey report aside for now.

120
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:34,870
Do you dare to play one-on-one?

121
00:09:34,870 --> 00:09:36,180
One shot, winner takes it all.

122
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:36,850
If you lose,

123
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:38,600
you give me half your ball possession.

124
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:39,720
What if you lose?

125
00:09:42,850 --> 00:09:44,120
I'll leave the team.

126
00:09:46,510 --> 00:09:48,040
Stop it, Zhou Yunze.

127
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:50,190
I think we should've changed long ago.

128
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:51,960
Some are dating,

129
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:54,170
others are skipping practice
for interviews—

130
00:09:54,170 --> 00:09:56,700
no one's even focused
on basketball anymore.

131
00:09:57,220 --> 00:09:57,880
Gu Han,

132
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:00,740
I'm asking you, do you dare or not?

133
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:03,200
Ball.

134
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:04,240
Captain,

135
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:05,120
stop it.

136
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:05,600
Ball.

137
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:07,400
Captain.

138
00:11:02,170 --> 00:11:02,870
Alright, alright.

139
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:03,650
Don't take it too seriously.

140
00:11:03,650 --> 00:11:04,750
We still have to prepare
for the analysis match.

141
00:11:04,750 --> 00:11:05,280
Right?

142
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:06,640
Li is right.

143
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:11,810
-Zhou.
-Zhou Yunze.

144
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:13,560
Zhou Yunze.

145
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:15,280
Zhou Yunze.

146
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:33,440
Dismissed.

147
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:37,360
What a mess.

148
00:11:49,510 --> 00:11:50,510
[2011 College Professional
Basketball League]

149
00:11:50,530 --> 00:11:51,970
[2010 College Professional
Basketball League]

150
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:52,320
Jiangcheng University

151
00:11:51,990 --> 00:11:53,260
[2009 College Professional
Basketball League]

152
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,880
used to be a championship team.

153
00:11:53,290 --> 00:11:55,110
[2008 College Professional
Basketball League]

154
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,960
Led by legends like Pei Tian,

155
00:11:59,120 --> 00:12:00,040
the team won

156
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:05,160
the College Basketball League championship
for eight consecutive years.

157
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:09,280
Unfortunately,
once that golden generation graduated,

158
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:10,960
Jiangcheng University fell into a slump.

159
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:13,720
We couldn't even make it
to the national tournament.

160
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:15,960
Then people like Li Sirui and I enrolled.

161
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:17,690
Everyone had high hopes for us.

162
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,280
Yet for two years running,

163
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:21,610
we were still stuck in the quarterfinals.

164
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:29,370
I'm about to be a senior.

165
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:31,320
This will be my last year

166
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:34,520
playing in the college
professional basketball league.

167
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:38,570
I must bring back the championship

168
00:12:38,680 --> 00:12:40,340
Jiangcheng University lost.

169
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:53,190
["Rising from the Noise,
Setting Sail Against the Odds"]

170
00:12:53,210 --> 00:12:54,960
[An Interview with Gu Han, Captain
of Jiangcheng University Basketball Team]

171
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:02,810
He is very strict with himself,

172
00:13:02,890 --> 00:13:04,680
and of course, with us too.

173
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:06,360
Deep down he's soft‑hearted, though.

174
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:08,720
He gives us red envelopes during holidays.

175
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:10,400
He doesn't talk much usually,

176
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:11,720
but when he's thoughtful,

177
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:12,800
he's like a girl.

178
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:15,080
Whoever marries him

179
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:17,360
will be extremely happy.

180
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:24,080
["Rising from the Noise,
Setting Sail Against the Odds"]

181
00:13:24,110 --> 00:13:25,550
[Exclusive Interview: Gu Han, Captain
of Jiangcheng University Basketball Team]

182
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:29,360
I've finished the survey report
you asked for.

183
00:13:29,760 --> 00:13:30,720
In exchange,

184
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:31,920
shouldn't you cooperate with me

185
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:34,050
to complete my interview assignment?

186
00:13:37,470 --> 00:13:38,120
["Rising from the Noise,
Setting Sail Against the Odds"]

187
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:38,940
[Exclusive Interview: Gu Han, Captain
of Jiangcheng University Basketball Team]

188
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:45,310
I must bring back the championship

189
00:13:45,310 --> 00:13:46,970
Jiangcheng University lost.

190
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:50,840
Actually, results

191
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:53,500
are never the only measure
of winning or losing.

192
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:56,300
The process of giving your all
is more precious.

193
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:59,020
This interview also inspired me.

194
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:00,400
It turns out

195
00:14:00,430 --> 00:14:01,440
that finding a goal

196
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:04,360
and fighting for it is the happiest thing.

197
00:14:07,570 --> 00:14:09,310
[Jiangcheng University TV Station]

198
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:16,800
Hello, Senior.

199
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:17,600
Hello.

200
00:14:20,130 --> 00:14:21,040
Xiangxiang,

201
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:22,760
isn't this your idol, Lin Hong?

202
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:24,300
Welcome back to your alma mater.

203
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:24,800
Let's go.

204
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:25,680
This way, please.

205
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:27,480
[Jiangcheng University TV Station]

206
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:29,840
Xiangxiang,

207
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:30,680
where are you going?

208
00:14:30,680 --> 00:14:31,520
Save me a seat.

209
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:32,720
I'll be right back.

210
00:14:33,550 --> 00:14:35,170
[Jiangcheng University TV Station]

211
00:14:35,370 --> 00:14:37,490
[No Staying Up Late]

212
00:14:38,450 --> 00:14:40,090
[No Staying Up Late]

213
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:47,400
Please welcome the famous host

214
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:49,560
and our honored
Jiangcheng University alumna,

215
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:51,020
Senior Lin Hong, to the stage.

216
00:14:51,020 --> 00:14:51,990
Please give her

217
00:14:52,020 --> 00:14:53,300
a round of applause.

218
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:58,040
Hello, juniors.

219
00:14:58,040 --> 00:14:59,640
I am Lin Hong.

220
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:01,440
I'm very happy to be back

221
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:02,480
at our campus TV station

222
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:04,000
to chat with all of you.

223
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:05,900
Welcome, Senior Lin Hong.

224
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:09,580
Xiangxiang.
This is your idol of many years.

225
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:12,570
Actually,

226
00:15:12,590 --> 00:15:13,680
when I first

227
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:15,450
got into hosting,

228
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:18,120
it was at our campus TV station's gala.

229
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:19,560
I think the young hosts

230
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:21,320
at our school

231
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:24,100
really have a higher starting point
than we did.

232
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:25,840
I'm really looking forward to your future.

233
00:15:25,620 --> 00:15:28,050
[Sharing Brilliant Lives: Jiangcheng
University Distinguished Alumni Talk]

234
00:15:30,560 --> 00:15:31,280
Next,

235
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:33,160
let's open the floor to the juniors

236
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:34,080
in the audience.

237
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:36,480
Feel free to ask
Senior Lin Hong questions.

238
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,720
Hello, Senior Lin Hong.

239
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:40,520
I've watched all your shows.

240
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:41,880
I really like you.

241
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:44,400
I'm so happy to meet you in person today.

242
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:45,320
Thank you,

243
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:46,320
Xiangxiang.

244
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:48,320
My question is,

245
00:15:49,160 --> 00:15:51,880
when you first started hosting,

246
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:54,560
did you feel nervous?

247
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,120
If so,

248
00:15:57,140 --> 00:15:58,720
how did you overcome it?

249
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:04,160
That's actually

250
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:06,370
a really good question.

251
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:10,280
If you want to be a host,

252
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:13,080
the first thing you need to be clear about

253
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:15,260
is why you're standing on this stage.

254
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:16,760
Is it because of

255
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:19,440
your dream,

256
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:21,250
or fame and fortune?

257
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:24,160
Only when you're firm enough inside,

258
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:26,330
will all the external problems

259
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:28,960
stop affecting you.

260
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:32,080
Of course, if you are really nervous,

261
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:34,840
you can calm yourself down,

262
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:36,620
and tell yourself:

263
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:39,000
I can do this.

264
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:44,260
Thank you, Senior.

265
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:21,599
Why is it you?

266
00:17:21,599 --> 00:17:22,440
Get up first.

267
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:24,079
Sorry, sorry.

268
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,320
Let me see.

269
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:46,360
[Campus Infirmary]

270
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:57,760
How is his hand?

271
00:17:57,960 --> 00:17:59,040
It's a muscle contusion.

272
00:17:59,040 --> 00:18:00,080
He needs to rest for a few days.

273
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:01,160
Take this medicine.

274
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:02,110
Three times a day.

275
00:18:02,110 --> 00:18:03,310
Right, don't forget.

276
00:18:03,690 --> 00:18:04,640
Thank you,

277
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:05,640
Dr. Ao.

278
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:09,280
I'm barely even a real doctor.

279
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,040
I don't mean to lecture you,

280
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:13,600
but couples should try not
to argue so much

281
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:14,700
and end up in the hospital.

282
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:15,560
Right.

283
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:19,720
We are not a couple.

284
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:22,400
It's okay for you to argue,

285
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:24,040
but you have to know the limit.

286
00:18:24,040 --> 00:18:25,720
You have to keep it within limits.

287
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:27,720
Didn't I say we are not a couple?

288
00:18:29,360 --> 00:18:30,360
Actually, I think

289
00:18:30,370 --> 00:18:31,680
for a young couple like you,

290
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:33,600
it all comes down to how you communicate.

291
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:35,080
Communication is really important.

292
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:35,680
Keep in mind

293
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,480
that you need to communicate
with him reasonably.

294
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:37,920
You know?

295
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:39,840
Are you really a medical student?

296
00:18:41,080 --> 00:18:41,610
Yes, I am.

297
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:43,280
I might need

298
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:44,160
to improve my general medical skills,

299
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:46,150
but when it comes to relationship advice,

300
00:18:46,150 --> 00:18:47,350
you can all come to me.

301
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:48,440
Thank you.

302
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:53,010
You're welcome.

303
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:03,000
I'm sorry.

304
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:05,920
It's all my fault you got hurt.

305
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:07,920
You have a game coming up.

306
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:09,720
How about

307
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:12,520
I make it up to you somehow?

308
00:19:12,550 --> 00:19:13,960
Just let me know.

309
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:35,960
Veggies.

310
00:19:50,840 --> 00:19:52,440
Can you finish it in one bite?

311
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:56,660
Okay, okay.

312
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,120
Look at those two.

313
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:15,280
They're showing off too much.

314
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,480
Egg.

315
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:43,680
Where's the soup?

316
00:21:20,840 --> 00:21:23,600
Who is it this early in the morning?

317
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:28,600
So noisy. Whose phone is this?

318
00:21:32,470 --> 00:21:36,190
[Gu Han]

319
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:39,560
Emergency.

320
00:21:39,790 --> 00:21:40,850
Come over quickly.

321
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:43,080
Emergency?

322
00:21:43,080 --> 00:21:44,920
What is he up to now?

323
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:04,200
What's the emergency?

324
00:22:05,130 --> 00:22:06,000
Close the door.

325
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:11,500
Change your shoes.

326
00:22:21,360 --> 00:22:22,420
I ordered takeout,

327
00:22:22,840 --> 00:22:24,170
but I can't open the box.

328
00:22:26,440 --> 00:22:27,520
That's it?

329
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:30,200
I thought something serious happened.

330
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:45,840
All right.

331
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:47,480
Leaving?

332
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:50,620
Fine, go ahead.

333
00:23:15,140 --> 00:23:16,040
Green beans.

334
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:29,480
Green beans.

335
00:23:33,880 --> 00:23:35,760
Just eat whatever I feed you.

336
00:23:35,930 --> 00:23:37,870
You ordered it yourself,
and you're still picky?

337
00:23:37,870 --> 00:23:38,800
Open your mouth.

338
00:23:46,280 --> 00:23:47,200
Have some rice.

339
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:50,960
I'm full.

340
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:04,040
You didn't wipe it clean.

341
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:11,680
What?

342
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:13,400
My head is a little itchy.

343
00:24:13,480 --> 00:24:14,720
Then scratch it.

344
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:18,440
I want to wash my hair.

345
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:27,840
Gu Han.

346
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:30,730
You're pushing your luck, aren't you?

347
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:41,960
Be gentle.

348
00:24:50,670 --> 00:24:51,870
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

349
00:24:51,880 --> 00:24:53,480
Sorry, let me wipe it for you.

350
00:25:07,040 --> 00:25:07,840
Keep going.

351
00:25:37,210 --> 00:25:38,240
Is it fun?

352
00:25:51,520 --> 00:25:53,480
I'll head back if there's nothing else.

353
00:25:53,480 --> 00:25:54,340
Shave my beard.

354
00:25:59,200 --> 00:26:00,280
Do you have a beard?

355
00:26:00,500 --> 00:26:01,400
Stubble.

356
00:27:01,890 --> 00:27:02,760
Wait.

357
00:27:05,130 --> 00:27:06,480
Now what?

358
00:27:06,880 --> 00:27:08,880
The kitchen hasn't been cleaned up.

359
00:27:09,320 --> 00:27:10,120
I already did.

360
00:27:13,080 --> 00:27:14,880
The bathroom floor is still wet.

361
00:27:15,280 --> 00:27:17,120
I wiped it.

362
00:27:30,020 --> 00:27:30,840
Mom.

363
00:27:33,260 --> 00:27:34,120
Hello, ma'am.

364
00:27:35,360 --> 00:27:36,760
I'm Gu Han's college classmate.

365
00:27:36,760 --> 00:27:37,520
He got injured recently,

366
00:27:37,520 --> 00:27:38,480
and I live nearby,

367
00:27:38,480 --> 00:27:39,880
so I came over to help out.

368
00:27:41,110 --> 00:27:42,080
Goodbye.

369
00:28:07,440 --> 00:28:09,000
If you hadn't gotten hurt because of me,

370
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:10,800
I wouldn't be doing this for you.

371
00:28:12,870 --> 00:28:13,800
Calm down.

372
00:28:14,450 --> 00:28:15,480
Just bear with it.

373
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:50,720
Today we're focusing on
the small-ball lineup.

374
00:28:50,720 --> 00:28:52,200
Remember your roles.

375
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:54,120
Pass more, run more.

376
00:28:54,480 --> 00:28:55,480
Come on!

377
00:28:56,040 --> 00:28:57,200
-Come on!
-Go!

378
00:29:00,800 --> 00:29:03,400
You can't even play,
but you still insist on watching.

379
00:29:03,400 --> 00:29:04,800
Get organized.

380
00:29:06,650 --> 00:29:07,560
Nice shot.

381
00:29:09,210 --> 00:29:11,800
Am I your personal sidekick now?

382
00:29:12,640 --> 00:29:13,900
Keep an eye on your man.

383
00:29:15,530 --> 00:29:16,560
Run, run!

384
00:29:17,440 --> 00:29:19,840
Do you think our team will win?

385
00:29:20,260 --> 00:29:21,240
Wanna make a bet?

386
00:29:21,280 --> 00:29:22,140
Bet on the half.

387
00:29:22,280 --> 00:29:24,400
If I win, you let me go back to sleep.

388
00:29:24,850 --> 00:29:26,980
I bet Jiangcheng University will win.

389
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:28,600
Watch the pace.

390
00:29:28,620 --> 00:29:29,280
Nice shot.

391
00:29:31,640 --> 00:29:32,520
Quick, quick, quick.

392
00:29:32,520 --> 00:29:33,220
Get back on defense!

393
00:29:33,220 --> 00:29:33,930
Defense!

394
00:29:33,960 --> 00:29:34,600
Get back on defense!

395
00:29:34,600 --> 00:29:35,680
Hurry back on defense!

396
00:29:35,680 --> 00:29:37,080
Protect the paint!

397
00:29:37,130 --> 00:29:38,280
[02:02]

398
00:29:38,160 --> 00:29:39,440
Okay, here we go.

399
00:29:40,730 --> 00:29:41,200
[Jiangcheng University Basketball Team]

400
00:29:41,320 --> 00:29:43,360
Hurry, outside!

401
00:29:44,120 --> 00:29:44,640
Good.

402
00:29:48,570 --> 00:29:49,780
[23:24]

403
00:29:50,320 --> 00:29:51,240
Hurry up.

404
00:29:51,240 --> 00:29:52,000
Go back.

405
00:29:51,530 --> 00:29:52,800
[39:44]

406
00:29:52,020 --> 00:29:52,840
Keep up.

407
00:29:52,860 --> 00:29:54,040
Everyone follow up!

408
00:29:55,200 --> 00:29:56,490
[Jiangcheng University Basketball Team]

409
00:29:55,700 --> 00:29:56,230
Rebound!

410
00:30:01,240 --> 00:30:02,100
Rebound!

411
00:30:03,920 --> 00:30:04,540
[48:65]

412
00:30:04,610 --> 00:30:06,510
[Jiangcheng University Basketball Team]

413
00:30:04,930 --> 00:30:05,800
Come here.

414
00:30:08,020 --> 00:30:09,260
Go to Jiangcheng Book Building

415
00:30:09,260 --> 00:30:10,280
and buy me a book.

416
00:30:10,300 --> 00:30:11,000
Now?

417
00:30:11,350 --> 00:30:12,560
It's so far.

418
00:30:13,060 --> 00:30:13,990
Who are you protecting?

419
00:30:13,990 --> 00:30:15,100
I need it for tomorrow's research class.

420
00:30:15,100 --> 00:30:16,320
It's urgent. Hurry.

421
00:30:16,400 --> 00:30:18,400
Speed up the pace in the second half.

422
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:20,280
Everyone needs to create space.

423
00:30:20,840 --> 00:30:22,100
Don't get locked down.

424
00:30:24,600 --> 00:30:26,460
Same tactics for the second half.

425
00:30:26,480 --> 00:30:27,740
Stay sharp, everyone.

426
00:30:28,450 --> 00:30:30,960
Keep steady offensive rhythm, don't rush.

427
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:32,920
You all good on stamina
for the second half?

428
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:33,920
-No problem.
-No problem.

429
00:30:33,920 --> 00:30:34,590
-No problem.
-No problem.

430
00:30:34,590 --> 00:30:35,380
-Coach.
-Next...

431
00:30:35,380 --> 00:30:36,200
I can play.

432
00:30:40,070 --> 00:30:41,720
One last time.

433
00:30:46,250 --> 00:30:46,600
[Come worship me for sneaking off
to film the Mr. Handsome contest]

434
00:30:47,060 --> 00:30:47,640
Offense!

435
00:30:48,250 --> 00:30:49,240
Keep the rhythm.

436
00:30:49,240 --> 00:30:50,170
Hurry, Captain.

437
00:30:50,720 --> 00:30:51,360
Get ready.

438
00:30:51,380 --> 00:30:52,960
Steady. Steady.

439
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:54,040
Steady.

440
00:30:54,080 --> 00:30:55,640
Don't rush.

441
00:30:56,850 --> 00:30:58,100
Sir, please turn around.

442
00:30:58,100 --> 00:30:59,720
[Chenguang Road]

443
00:31:00,080 --> 00:31:00,880
Let's go.

444
00:31:08,010 --> 00:31:09,040
What's wrong?

445
00:31:09,040 --> 00:31:10,150
What's going on?

446
00:31:25,280 --> 00:31:27,520
Got the book? That was pretty fast.

447
00:31:28,560 --> 00:31:30,160
Your hand healed even faster.
